sa2-recomp local patch 0001 to SDL 3.4.16: border addressing and depth clamp

    NOT FROM THE SDL PROJECT. This patch belongs to the SA2 Recompiled
    project and was written for it by an AI agent (Claude). It is not
    submitted to SDL and is not meant for submission: the user's rulings of
    2026-10-04 (Documentation/decisions/2026-10-04-S5-user-rulings.md,
    ruling 3, as amended by
    Documentation/decisions/2026-10-04-S5-user-rulings-2.md) keep it in the
    project, which applies it at every build.

    Target: SDL release 3.4.16 (tag release-3.4.16), commit
    fa2c02bb6e21974a89ea9824bc53c9932abe5f9c, the commit the release
    tarball records in its own .git-hash file (its REVISION.txt reads
    "release-3.4.16-0-gfa2c02bb6"). The tarball is SDL3-3.4.16.tar.gz,
    sha256 7322236cd12090c3eb40b9728be4d49c76f66ad17d04369584d4ecad5cf77c68.

    What it changes:

    - Border addressing. A fourth sampler address mode,
      SDL_GPU_SAMPLERADDRESSMODE_CLAMP_TO_BORDER (value 3), with the border
      color chosen through
      SDL_PROP_GPU_SAMPLER_CREATE_SA2RECOMP_BORDER_COLOR_NUMBER: transparent
      black (the default), opaque black or opaque white.
    - Depth clamp. SDL_PROP_GPU_GRAPHICSPIPELINE_CREATE_SA2RECOMP_DEPTH_CLAMP_BOOLEAN
      clamps depth to the viewport's depth range while depth clip stays
      enabled, as Direct3D does.
    - Two device properties report support:
      SDL_PROP_GPU_DEVICE_SA2RECOMP_SAMPLER_CLAMP_TO_BORDER_BOOLEAN and
      SDL_PROP_GPU_DEVICE_SA2RECOMP_DEPTH_CLIP_AND_CLAMP_BOOLEAN.

    Every new property lives in a local namespace ("SDL.gpu.*.sa2recomp.*").
    A stock or system SDL3 never sets them, so they read false there, and
    that is how a build on stock SDL takes its shader fallback. Address
    mode 3 means CLAMP_TO_BORDER only where the border property reads true.
    No struct layout changes and no new functions.

    Per backend:

    - Vulkan: CLAMP_TO_BORDER and the three float border colors are core
      1.0. Depth clamp with clip enables VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable, and its
      depthClipEnable feature, only when the device reports the feature and
      depth clamping is requested, and then chains
      VkPipelineRasterizationDepthClipStateCreateInfoEXT.
    - D3D12: D3D12_TEXTURE_ADDRESS_MODE_BORDER with BorderColor. D3D12
      already clamps depth with DepthClipEnable on, so the pipeline needs
      no change and the clip-and-clamp property is always true.
    - Metal: MTLSamplerAddressModeClampToBorderColor on macOS only.
      MTLDepthClipMode is clip or clamp, never both, so Metal reports no
      depth clamp with clip and refuses the pipeline property.

    In debug mode SDL_CreateGPUSampler checks the address modes and the
    border color, and both creation functions refuse a feature the device
    does not report.

    Marked as modified (zlib licence, clause 2): the build configures SDL
    with -DSDL_VENDOR_INFO="sa2-recomp sdl3-patches <id>", so
    SDL_GetRevision() reads
    "SDL-release-3.4.16-0-gfa2c02bb6 (sa2-recomp sdl3-patches <id>)".
    <id> is the first 12 hex digits of the sha256 of L, where L is, for
    each patch file in order, its sha256 as 64 lowercase hex digits
    followed by one newline byte (0x0a). With this patch alone:

      printf '%s\n' "$(sha256sum 0001-*.patch | cut -c1-64)" | sha256sum | cut -c1-12

    How to apply it: strictly, in the top directory of the extracted
    tarball, with GNU patch in the C locale,

      LC_ALL=C patch -p1 --fuzz=0 --forward --batch < 0001-gpu-clamp-to-border-and-depth-clamp-with-clip.patch

    and refuse the result if patch reports any hunk "succeeded at ...
    (offset ...)": --fuzz=0 still lets GNU patch place a hunk at an offset,
    and this patch, made against the pinned tarball, never needs one. The
    project's build does exactly this (tools/s5/sdl3_patches.py) and also
    refuses an apply that leaves a file it names unchanged. git apply is
    not an equal alternative: it places a hunk at an offset without saying
    so. Check the result as well as the exit status: afterwards
    include/SDL3/SDL_gpu.h defines
    SDL_PROP_GPU_DEVICE_SA2RECOMP_SAMPLER_CLAMP_TO_BORDER_BOOLEAN.

